1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,609
Last time, you wrote one lead.

2
00:00:03,509 --> 00:00:06,552
Today that lead becomes a whole evening,

3
00:00:07,002 --> 00:00:11,350
with a beginning, something to do, a moment of danger,

4
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:15,278
and a reason to come back next week.

5
00:00:17,078 --> 00:00:18,817
It takes three records,

6
00:00:19,267 --> 00:00:21,876
and one line on a landmark.

7
00:00:23,076 --> 00:00:26,554
An evening at a table has four parts.

8
00:00:28,354 --> 00:00:35,746
The open is where the crew's told where to go, and why it has to be tonight.

9
00:00:36,646 --> 00:00:42,733
The objective is the one thing they have to do when they get there.

10
00:00:43,633 --> 00:00:47,546
The climax is the moment it could go wrong.

11
00:00:48,446 --> 00:00:52,359
And the hook is the last thing they learn,

12
00:00:52,809 --> 00:00:55,417
which is why they come back.

13
00:00:57,217 --> 00:00:59,826
I've put minutes beside each one.

14
00:01:00,726 --> 00:01:03,770
Those are a plan, not a measurement,

15
00:01:04,220 --> 00:01:08,133
and you'll time a real table against them later.

16
00:01:09,333 --> 00:01:13,246
Here's something to be clear about before we build.

17
00:01:14,146 --> 00:01:18,059
The game has no idea what an evening is.

18
00:01:19,859 --> 00:01:22,467
There's no end of session screen.

19
00:01:22,917 --> 00:01:25,526
There's no recap of last week.

20
00:01:26,426 --> 00:01:30,774
And there's no timer that stops you at forty-five minutes.

21
00:01:32,574 --> 00:01:35,183
So you do all three yourself,

22
00:01:35,633 --> 00:01:38,241
with the shape of the episode.

23
00:01:39,141 --> 00:01:43,489
The last step ends at home, and you stop there.

24
00:01:44,389 --> 00:01:46,998
The open lead is your recap.

25
00:01:47,898 --> 00:01:50,941
And the time limit is your watch.

26
00:01:52,141 --> 00:01:54,315
Before any records, the sheet.

27
00:01:55,215 --> 00:01:58,693
It's a small table in your campaign page,

28
00:01:59,143 --> 00:02:02,622
one row for each of the four parts.

29
00:02:04,422 --> 00:02:07,030
Then a few lines under it.

30
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:11,393
What the crew learns. What it pays. Who's busy.

31
00:02:12,293 --> 00:02:14,467
And where the evening ends.

32
00:02:16,267 --> 00:02:19,311
Fill in what the crew learns first.

33
00:02:20,211 --> 00:02:22,820
If you can't, it's a trip,

34
00:02:23,270 --> 00:02:25,009
and not an episode.

35
00:02:26,209 --> 00:02:28,383
Now for the records themselves.

36
00:02:29,283 --> 00:02:32,761
The open is the lead you already have.

37
00:02:33,211 --> 00:02:35,385
It gets one more line,

38
00:02:35,835 --> 00:02:39,313
so that finishing it shows the next step.

39
00:02:41,113 --> 00:02:43,722
The next step is the objective.

40
00:02:44,172 --> 00:02:46,346
Science reads the Wren's log.

41
00:02:48,146 --> 00:02:50,754
Two things I measured about that.

42
00:02:51,654 --> 00:02:54,698
Any dead ship in the system counts,

43
00:02:55,148 --> 00:02:59,930
and the game may have put one of its own there.

44
00:03:00,830 --> 00:03:04,743
So write the text so either one makes sense.

45
00:03:05,643 --> 00:03:09,122
And the step's hidden until the crew arrives,

46
00:03:09,572 --> 00:03:12,180
so nothing they scanned earlier counts.

47
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:16,424
The climax isn't a step at all.

48
00:03:16,874 --> 00:03:19,048
It's something at the place.

49
00:03:20,848 --> 00:03:23,022
One line on the landmark,

50
00:03:23,472 --> 00:03:27,385
and three ships are waiting when the crew arrives.

51
00:03:29,185 --> 00:03:31,793
And notice what I haven't written.

52
00:03:32,693 --> 00:03:34,433
Nothing says, destroy them.

53
00:03:35,333 --> 00:03:38,376
So the crew has a real choice.

54
00:03:38,826 --> 00:03:43,174
They can fight. They can scan under fire and run.

55
00:03:44,074 --> 00:03:47,987
Or they can leave, and come back next week,

56
00:03:48,437 --> 00:03:51,480
and the guards will be there again.

57
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:56,159
Last, the way home, and next week's lead.

58
00:03:57,959 --> 00:04:02,741
The home step ends when the ship's back at the relay,

59
00:04:03,191 --> 00:04:05,365
and that's where it pays.

60
00:04:06,265 --> 00:04:10,613
A crew that's just been paid, at their own station,

61
00:04:11,063 --> 00:04:14,107
is a crew you can send home.

62
00:04:15,907 --> 00:04:19,820
And the moment it's done, the next lead appears.

63
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:25,502
That's the hook, and it's the last thing they read tonight.

64
00:04:27,302 --> 00:04:29,911
And next week, after they continue,

65
00:04:30,361 --> 00:04:33,839
it's the one open line of the campaign.

66
00:04:34,739 --> 00:04:37,348
So it's the recap as well.

67
00:04:38,548 --> 00:04:40,722
Save, lint, and it's clean.

68
00:04:41,622 --> 00:04:43,361
So let's play it.

69
00:04:45,161 --> 00:04:49,509
One line of the campaign in the log, not three.

70
00:04:50,409 --> 00:04:52,148
I engage the lead,

71
00:04:52,598 --> 00:04:55,641
and here's the Wren, and the warning.

72
00:04:57,441 --> 00:05:00,920
Science scans her, and the way home appears,

73
00:05:01,370 --> 00:05:03,978
so I engage that as well.

74
00:05:05,778 --> 00:05:07,517
We're home, we're paid,

75
00:05:07,967 --> 00:05:10,141
and there's the second boat.

76
00:05:11,041 --> 00:05:13,215
And that's the whole evening.

77
00:05:15,015 --> 00:05:18,928
Now I close the game and start it again.

78
00:05:19,828 --> 00:05:22,437
And the hook's still there, waiting.

79
00:05:23,637 --> 00:05:27,550
So an evening is four parts and three records.

80
00:05:29,350 --> 00:05:32,393
You end it, because the game won't.

81
00:05:33,293 --> 00:05:36,337
And a step that's done stays done,

82
00:05:36,787 --> 00:05:40,265
so a long evening is simply two evenings.

83
00:05:42,065 --> 00:05:45,978
Next time, we turn this one into a pattern,

84
00:05:46,428 --> 00:05:51,211
and write the second evening in a quarter of the time.
